{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01RS5ae3YcVJveT6rQAg1AD2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **Q17: Feature scaling — normalization vs standardization** (`answers/06-017-feature-scaling-normalization-vs-standardization.md`).\n\nKey content:\n\n- **Decision framework:** min-max for bounded/known ranges (pixel intensities, ratings) → z-score standardization for general continuous features → robust scaling when heavy outliers exist → no scaling for tree-based models (XGBoost/LightGBM are rank-invariant)\n- **Critical production rule:** fit scaler on training data only; use sklearn `Pipeline` to prevent test-set leakage\n- **Concrete examples:** fraud-detection SVM with transaction-amount dominance fixed by StandardScaler; CNN pixel normalization with min-max; at-serving-time scaler serialization and drift monitoring\n- **Pitfalls:** fitting on full dataset (leakage), applying min-max when outliers exist at inference time, unnecessary scaling of tree models"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":70138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":267,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e14f7907-af43-4c29-b968-235d1d1494d9","uuid":"dc4c692d-eb40-4c61-9a99-73220b379d86"}
